# Complete narrated tutorial of the current tool

Status: DONE
Milestone: Local video, captions and chapter navigation
Dependencies: 15_USER_GUIDE.todo (existing preview guidance), 57_KEYBOARD_CONTROLS.todo, 59_PREVIOUS_ANSWER_CONTEXT.todo

## Request

The October10 22:12 request asks for a full tutorial covering every part of the tool
with visible clicks. Deliver a usable video, not merely a storyboard or slide deck.

## Scope

- [x] Inventory the current controls, source/installed differences and operational boundaries.
- [x] Author a complete sequence covering installation, window controls, audio device cards,
  transcription, question selection/editing/snapshots, providers, streaming answers, previous
  answer, clarification, notes/files, exports, all keyboard modes, recovery and diagnostics.
- [x] Capture actual WPF state transitions from an isolated copy with unchanged production XAML.
  Use scripted routed input and explicit sample IO, not an owner's desktop or real meeting.
- [x] Generate offline synthetic narration and word-timed captions.
- [x] Encode the final readable landscape video with truthful action cues and chapters.
- [x] Review encoded action/result states, narration alignment, completeness and player behavior.
- [x] Deliver the MP4 and offline chaptered player, retain provenance, and update completion records.

## Boundaries

- This is a scripted tutorial, not an OS mouse recording, live-recognition benchmark or model-quality test.
- Audio events, endpoint labels and provider responses are synthetic. Clipboard output goes to an
  isolated sink; file writes use throwaway examples. Native file pickers are omitted and described.
- Installation, provider provisioning and Windows settings are labelled instructional inserts,
  not evidence that installation, account setup or a live service operation was executed.
- Current-source Previous answer remains absent from the unchanged published v0.2.0-preview.1.
- No real audio/model request, owner-window restart, new installer, commit, push or upload is implied.

